+# Harness-side patches
+
+Patches here target the **dsh** source tree (`deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness`), not
+this plugin. They are the general-purpose extension points the plugin's shipped
+capabilities prefer when the host provides them. **The plugin runs without
+them**: every patched capability has a documented fallback, and a host that
+carries none of these patches still gets the full Settings → 技能 surface.
+
+Apply from the harness checkout root, on the matching release tag:
+
+```bash
+git apply /path/to/dsh-skill-hub/patches/<name>.patch
+```
+
+| Patch | Target release | Capability it completes | Fallback without it |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `input-trigger-candidate-decorations.patch` | `dsh-v0.1.7-alpha.1` | `/`-menu invocation dots (`dotModelColor` / `dotUserColor`) through the official candidate contract: `ctx.inputTriggers.decorateSource` re-presents a foreign source's rows, and the returned `icon` component renders in the menu row. | `src/client/slash-dots.tsx` wraps the registered `/skill` source through the private source roster and injects the dot into the rendered option list (hashed CSS class, with a `[role="listbox"]` retry). Dots are cosmetic: a host whose internals moved shows no dots and the catalog keeps working. |
+
+The patch keeps the undecorated pipeline byte-for-byte in step with the release:
+a source with no registered pass settles in its own turn, and only registered
+decoration defers the group until the passes resolve. Verified against
+`dsh-v0.1.7-alpha.1`: it applies cleanly to a pristine tag checkout and
+reproduces the applied working tree, the package's own client suite passes
+(71/71 unpatched, 73/73 patched — the two added specs cover async decoration
+with disposal and throwing-decorator containment), and `tsc --strict` over the
+changed files reports the same single pre-existing spec diagnostic as the
+unpatched tree.
+
+Background, the upstream request trail, and the full patch text live in
+`.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/input-trigger-candidate-decorations/report.md`.
